Tracking systems create visibility and accountability for products moving through reverse supply chains, enabling optimization of logistics, assessment of recovery rates, and identification of process bottlenecks. Physical tracking through barcodes, RFID, or other identifiers allows accurate data collection on product volumes, conditions, and recovery outcomes. Digital tracking systems integrate with refurbishment facilities, enabling real-time visibility into product flow. From a design perspective, products must accommodate tracking technologies without compromising aesthetics or functionality.